  "summary": "Daniel Ferreira (pt-0015): contrast CT placed and RBC-RAD-07 prep done for his Mon 10/26 09:00 slot.\n- CT order: CT abdomen and pelvis with IV contrast (sr-t0001), booked for 10/26 09:00 and linked to the appointment (appt-t5-1026), as §5 requires. It's for surveillance of his pancreatic cyst, pancreatic protocol per GI.\n- Contrast allergy (§1/§2): his 2019 iohexol reaction was moderate (hives and mild eyelid swelling) according to the radiology report written that day. The \"anaphylaxis\" entry on his allergy list came from his own account in 2021, so it doesn't change the grade. I left that entry unchanged. His shellfish and Betadine allergies aren't risk factors. Premedication ordered, by mouth:\n  - Prednisone 50 mg Sun 10/25 at 20:00, Mon 10/26 at 02:00 and at 08:00 (mr-t0003)\n  - Diphenhydramine 50 mg Mon 10/26 at 08:00 (mr-t0004)\n  He has been told he needs a driver.\n- Kidney function (§4): he's 64 and diabetic, so he needs a creatinine within 30 days before the scan. His 9/24 result is more than 30 days out. His ED results from 10/16–17 (1.94 falling to 1.46) were drawn during kidney injury (AKI) and don't count. New creatinine ordered (sr-t0002), to be drawn between now and Mon 10/26 08:00. The scan stays as booked; the radiologist reviews the result that day.\n- Metformin (§6): the ED summary documents AKI, so I put metformin on hold (mr-t5-metformin). He takes his last dose Sun evening and skips it the day of the scan and for 48 h after. It restarts only once a recheck is normal. That recheck creatinine is ordered for 10/28–10/30 (sr-t0006).\n- Follow-up task for you, due 10/30 (task-t0008): review the post-scan creatinine and restart metformin if it's normal. It also asks you to confirm the pre-scan creatinine was drawn before the scan.\n- Patient told by portal message (comm-t0007): when to get both blood tests, exact pill times, needs a driver, metformin hold, arrive 08:45, drink fluids, warning signs.\n- Progress note written and signed, citing RBC-RAD-07 (doc-t0009).",
